course: dictionary
lesson: 3166
title: Emotional: words about feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Emotional» means about feelings. Emotional health means looking after how you feel, just as physical health means looking after your body.
explain: An emotional person shows strong feelings easily, such as crying or getting excited. «Straight after a match children are tired and emotional, so a list of mistakes in the car lands much harder.» The children have big feelings after the match, so a list of mistakes hurts them more.
explain: An emotional event or story makes people feel strong feelings. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: if «full of strong feelings» fits, you have the right meaning.
fact: Emotional means about feelings, as in emotional wellbeing: looking after your feelings as well as your body.
fact: An emotional person shows strong feelings easily, such as crying or getting excited.
fact: An emotional moment or story makes people feel strong feelings.
fact: Useful phrases: get emotional, emotional support, emotional moment.
fact: «Tired and emotional» is a British joke that means drunk. Newspapers once used it as a polite way of describing a politician who had been drinking.
exercise: In PSHE lessons you learn about emotional wellbeing. What does emotional mean here? | About the weather | About sport only | About numbers | *About feelings
exercise: After the match the children were tired and emotional. Find and copy one word that means about feelings. | children | match | *emotional | list
exercise: Lily cried and cheered at the end of the film. She is an emotional person. What does this mean? | She can run very fast | She is always cold | *She shows strong feelings easily | She never watches films
test: «The goodbye at the station was an emotional moment.» What does emotional mean here? | Very cheap | Very quiet and calm | *Full of strong feelings | Covered in mud
test: Which phrase means someone needs care for their feelings? | physical sport | *emotional support | bright light | loud noise
exam: Which sentence uses emotionally correctly? | Emotionally, the sky is green. | The emotionally bus was late. | She emotionally ran very fast. | *She spoke emotionally about the sad story.
